 >Password retrieved from RAM is a well known issue :)

No, it is a Bios problem, and most manufacturers are vulnerable, so it=20
is definitly
not a "well known issue". We are not talking about a typical userland=20
application using
a weak primitive like getpassword() here, but of a misusage of the BIOS A=
pi.
(cf attached whitepaper for information).

Anyway, I agree the problem doesnt lie in your software but in the swap=20
encryption
like Nigel mentioned. If you could help me track which versions of the=20
kernel using dm-crypt
were vulnerable, that would help me a lot.

Regards,

Jonathan-

